SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION (SRS)

Hospital Management System

Project Category: Web Application
Frontend: React + TypeScript
Backend: ASP.NET Core Web API
Database: Microsoft SQL Server
ORM: Entity Framework Core
Authentication: ASP.NET Core Identity + JWT

⸻

1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

The Hospital Management System is a web-based application designed to help hospitals manage patient information, appointments, medical records and other hospital activities digitally.

The system will replace or reduce the use of paper-based records and make it easier for hospital staff and patients to access the information they need.

This SRS explains what the system should do and what each project team is expected to work on.

⸻

2. Problem Statement

Many hospitals still depend on manual and paper-based processes.

This can result in:

* Loss or misplacement of patient records
* Long waiting times during patient registration
* Difficulty managing appointments
* Difficulty accessing patient medical history
* Poor coordination between hospital staff
* Inefficient management of hospital activities

The proposed system will provide one centralized platform for managing these activities.

⸻

3. Objectives

The system should:

1. Allow patients to be registered and managed digitally.
2. Allow patients to book and manage appointments.
3. Allow doctors and authorized staff to view relevant patient information.
4. Allow doctors to create and manage electronic medical records.
5. Provide different dashboards depending on the user’s role.
6. Secure patient and hospital information.
7. Reduce unnecessary paperwork.
8. Make hospital information easier to manage and access.

⸻

4. Target Users

The system will have the following main users:

4.1 Administrator

The administrator manages the overall system.

The administrator should be able to:

* Manage users
* Manage staff accounts
* Assign user roles
* View/manage patients
* View/manage doctors and other staff
* View appointments
* Manage basic hospital information
* Access administrative reports where applicable

4.2 Doctor

Doctors should be able to:

* Log into the system
* View their appointments
* View assigned/relevant patient information
* View a patient’s medical history
* Create medical records
* Update medical records
* Add diagnosis and treatment information
* Add prescriptions/medication information where applicable

4.3 Nurse

Nurses should be able to:

* Log into the system
* View relevant patient information
* View assigned/relevant appointments
* Access medical information they are authorized to see
* Update information they are permitted to update

4.4 Receptionist

Receptionists should be able to:

* Register patients
* Update patient information
* Schedule appointments
* View appointments
* Manage appointment status
* Search for patient records

4.5 Patient

Patients should be able to:

* Create/login to their account
* View their profile
* View their appointments
* Request/book appointments
* View appointment status
* View their available medical records
* Update permitted personal information

⸻

5. System Scope

The first version of the system will focus on:

* User authentication
* User roles and permissions
* Patient registration and management
* Doctor/staff management
* Appointment scheduling
* Electronic Medical Records (EMR)
* User dashboards
* Secure access to patient information

Features outside this scope can be considered future improvements.

⸻

6. Functional Requirements

6.1 User Registration and Authentication

The system must provide secure login and authentication.

Users should be able to:

* Log in with their credentials
* Log out
* Have their identity verified
* Access features based on their role

The system will use:

* ASP.NET Core Identity
* JWT authentication
* Role-based authorization

⸻

6.2 User Roles and Permissions

Each user must have an appropriate role.

Example:

Role	Main Access
Administrator	Full system management
Doctor	Patients, appointments and medical records
Nurse	Authorized patient and medical information
Receptionist	Patients and appointments
Patient	Own profile, appointments and permitted records

Users should not be able to access information or functions that their role does not permit.

⸻

7. Patient Management

The system must allow authorized staff to register and manage patients.

Patient information may include:

* Patient ID
* Full name
* Date of birth
* Gender
* Phone number
* Email
* Address
* Emergency contact
* Other necessary registration information

Authorized users should be able to:

* Create a patient
* View patient information
* Search for a patient
* Update patient information
* View the patient’s relevant history

⸻

8. Appointment Management

The system must allow appointments to be created and managed.

An appointment should contain information such as:

* Appointment ID
* Patient
* Doctor
* Date
* Time
* Reason for visit
* Appointment status

Possible appointment statuses include:

* Pending
* Confirmed
* Completed
* Cancelled

Patients

Patients should be able to request/book appointments where applicable.

Receptionists

Receptionists should be able to schedule and manage appointments.

Doctors

Doctors should be able to view their scheduled appointments.

⸻

9. Electronic Medical Records (EMR)

The system should allow authorized medical personnel to create and manage electronic medical records.

A medical record may contain:

* Patient
* Doctor
* Date
* Symptoms/complaint
* Diagnosis
* Treatment
* Prescription/medication
* Doctor’s notes
* Follow-up information

Medical records should be associated with the correct patient.

Only authorized users should be able to access or modify medical records.

⸻

