21. Non-Functional Requirements

21.1 Performance

The system should respond reasonably quickly to normal user requests.

21.2 Security

Only authorized users should access protected information.

21.3 Usability

The system should be simple enough for hospital staff and patients to understand and use.

21.4 Reliability

The system should handle normal operations without losing or incorrectly modifying information.

21.5 Maintainability

The code should be organized so that different team members can work on and maintain the system.

21.6 Scalability

The system should be structured in a way that allows additional hospital features to be added later.

⸻

22. Basic System Workflow

A typical patient workflow could be:

Patient registers/logs in → Patient requests appointment → Appointment is scheduled/confirmed → Doctor sees appointment → Doctor accesses patient information → Doctor creates/updates medical record → Patient can view permitted information.

A receptionist workflow could be:

Receptionist logs in → Searches/registers patient → Creates appointment → Updates appointment status.

A doctor workflow could be:

Doctor logs in → Views appointments → Selects patient → Views medical history → Creates/updates medical record.

An administrator workflow could be:

Administrator logs in → Views dashboard → Manages users/staff → Manages roles → Oversees hospital activities.

